{"id":"CVE-2025-26465","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"redhat","published":"2025-02-18T18:27:16.843Z","updated":"2026-11-05T15:26:48.485Z","title":"Openssh: machine-in-the-middle attack if verifyhostkeydns is enabled","description":"A vulnerability was found in OpenSSH when the VerifyHostKeyDNS option is enabled. A machine-in-the-middle attack can be performed by a malicious machine impersonating a legit server. This issue occurs due to how OpenSSH mishandles error codes in specific conditions when verifying the host key. For an attack to be considered successful, the attacker needs to manage to exhaust the client's memory resource first, turning the attack complexity high.","cwe":["CWE-390 Detection of Error Condition Without Action"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","other":"Red Hat severity rating","content":"{\"value\": \"Moderate\", \"namespace\": \"https://access.redhat.com/security/updates/classification/\"}"},{"src":"cna","v":"3.1","score":6.8,"sev":"MEDIUM","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"poc","Automatable":"no","Technical Impact":"total"}}],"affected":[{"packageName":"OpenSSH","collectionURL":"https://www.openssh.com/","repo":"https://anongit.mindrot.org/openssh.git","defaultStatus":"unaffected","versions":["affected 6.8p1 <=9.9p1 (custom)"]},{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 8","packageName":"openssh","collectionURL":"https://access.redhat.com/downloads/content/package-browser/","defaultStatus":"affected","cpes":["cpe:/a:redhat:enterprise_linux:8::appstream","cpe:/o:redhat:enterprise_linux:8::baseos"],"versions":["unaffected 0:8.0p1-26.el8_10 <* (rpm)"]},{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 8","packageName":"openssh","collectionURL":"https://access.redhat.com/downloads/content/package-browser/","defaultStatus":"affected","cpes":["cpe:/a:redhat:enterprise_linux:8::appstream","cpe:/o:redhat:enterprise_linux:8::baseos"],"versions":["unaffected 0:8.0p1-26.el8_10 <* (rpm)"]},{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9","packageName":"openssh","collectionURL":"https://access.redhat.com/downloads/content/package-browser/","defaultStatus":"affected","cpes":["cpe:/a:redhat:enterprise_linux:9::appstream","cpe:/o:redhat:enterprise_linux:9::baseos"],"versions":["unaffected 0:8.7p1-45.el9 <* (rpm)"]},{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9","packageName":"openssh","collectionURL":"https://access.redhat.com/downloads/content/package-browser/","defaultStatus":"affected","cpes":["cpe:/a:redhat:enterprise_linux:9::appstream","cpe:/o:redhat:enterprise_linux:9::baseos"],"versions":["unaffected 0:8.7p1-45.el9 <* (rpm)"]},{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9.4 Extended Update Support","packageName":"openssh","collectionURL":"https://access.redhat.com/downloads/content/package-browser/","defaultStatus":"affected","cpes":["cpe:/a:redhat:rhel_eus:9.4::appstream","cpe:/o:redhat:rhel_eus:9.4::baseos"],"versions":["unaffected 0:8.7p1-38.el9_4.5 <* (rpm)"]},{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat Discovery 1.14","packageName":"discovery/discovery-server-rhel9","collectionURL":"https://catalog.redhat.com/software/containers/","defaultStatus":"affected","cpes":["cpe:/a:redhat:discovery:1.14::el9"],"versions":["unaffected 1.14.3-1748529279 <* (rpm)"]},{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 10","packageName":"openssh","collectionURL":"https://access.redhat.com/downloads/content/package-browser/","defaultStatus":"unaffected","cpes":["cpe:/a:redhat:enterprise_linux:10"]},{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 6","packageName":"openssh","collectionURL":"https://access.redhat.com/downloads/content/package-browser/","defaultStatus":"unknown","cpes":["cpe:/o:redhat:rhel_els:6"]},{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 7","packageName":"openssh","collectionURL":"https://access.redhat.com/downloads/content/package-browser/","defaultStatus":"unknown","cpes":["cpe:/o:redhat:rhel_els:7"]},{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat OpenShift Container Platform 4","packageName":"openshift/ose-rhel-coreos-9","collectionURL":"https://access.redhat.com/downloads/content/package-browser/","defaultStatus":"affected","cpes":["cpe:/a:redhat:openshift:4"]},{"vendor":"Siemens","product":"SIDIS Secured SmartPlug","defaultStatus":"unknown","versions":["affected 0 <V7.26.0310 (custom)"]},{"vendor":"Siemens","product":"SIMATIC S7-1500 CPU 1518-4 PN/DP MFP","defaultStatus":"unknown","versions":["affected V3.1.5 <* (custom)"]},{"vendor":"Siemens","product":"SIMATIC S7-1500 CPU 1518F-4 PN/DP MFP","defaultStatus":"unknown","versions":["affected V3.1.5 <* (custom)"]},{"vendor":"Siemens","product":"SIPLUS S7-1500 CPU 1518-4 PN/DP MFP","defaultStatus":"unknown","versions":["affected V3.1.5 <* (custom)"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2025:16823","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2025:16823"},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2025:3837","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2025:3837"},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2025:6993","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2025:6993"},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2025:8385","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2025:8385"},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2025-26465","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_REDHAT"]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/solutions/7109879"},{"url":"https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2344780","tags":["issue-tracking","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHBZ#2344780"},{"url":"https://seclists.org/oss-sec/2025/q1/144"},{"url":"https://lists.debian.org/debian-lts-announce/2025/02/msg00020.html"},{"url":"https://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2025/02/18/1"},{"url":"https://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2025/02/18/4"},{"url":"https://www.theregister.com/2025/02/18/openssh_vulnerabilities_mitm_dos/"},{"url":"https://bugzilla.suse.com/show_bug.cgi?id=1237040"},{"url":"https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2025-26465"},{"url":"https://ftp.openbsd.org/pub/OpenBSD/patches/7.6/common/008_ssh.patch.sig"},{"url":"https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2025-26465"},{"url":"https://www.openssh.com/releasenotes.html#9.9p2"},{"url":"https://blog.qualys.com/vulnerabilities-threat-research/2025/02/18/qualys-tru-discovers-two-vulnerabilities-in-openssh-cve-2025-26465-cve-2025-26466"},{"url":"https://lists.mindrot.org/pipermail/openssh-unix-announce/2025-February/000161.html"},{"url":"https://security.netapp.com/advisory/ntap-20250228-0003/"},{"url":"https://www.vicarius.io/vsociety/posts/cve-2025-26465-detect-vulnerable-openssh"},{"url":"https://www.vicarius.io/vsociety/posts/cve-2025-26465-mitigate-vulnerable-openssh"},{"url":"http://seclists.org/fulldisclosure/2025/May/8"},{"url":"http://seclists.org/fulldisclosure/2025/May/7"},{"url":"http://seclists.org/fulldisclosure/2025/Feb/18"},{"url":"https://cert-portal.siemens.com/productcert/html/ssa-082556.html"},{"url":"https://cert-portal.siemens.com/productcert/html/ssa-585531.html"}],"workarounds":["This issue can be mitigated by disabling VerifyHostKeyDNS by setting that option to 'no' in an SSH client configuration file (such as /etc/ssh/ssh_config, ~/.ssh/config, or one of the files in the /etc/ssh/ssh_config.d/ directory). This is the default configuration in Red Hat Enterprise Linux.\n\nFor configurations that require VerifyHostKeyDNS to be enabled (set to either 'yes' or 'ask'), mitigation for this issue is either not available or the currently available options do not meet the Red Hat Product Security criteria comprising ease of use and deployment, applicability to widespread installation base or stability."],"vendors":["openssh"]}
{"id":"CVE-2025-26466","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"redhat","published":"2025-02-28T21:25:28.861Z","updated":"2026-11-05T15:26:53.478Z","title":"Openssh: denial-of-service in openssh","description":"A flaw was found in the OpenSSH package. For each ping packet the SSH server receives, a pong packet is allocated in a memory buffer and stored in a queue of packages. It is only freed when the server/client key exchange has finished. A malicious client may keep sending such packages, leading to an uncontrolled increase in memory consumption on the server side. Consequently, the server may become unavailable, resulting in a denial of service attack.","cwe":["CWE-770 Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","other":"Red Hat severity rating","content":"{\"value\": \"Moderate\", \"namespace\": \"https://access.redhat.com/security/updates/classification/\"}"},{"src":"cna","v":"3.1","score":5.9,"sev":"MEDIUM","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"poc","Automatable":"no","Technical Impact":"partial"}}],"affected":[{"packageName":"OpenSSH","collectionURL":"https://www.openssh.com/","repo":"https://anongit.mindrot.org/openssh.git","defaultStatus":"unaffected","versions":["affected 9.5p1 <=9.9p1 (custom)"]},{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 10","packageName":"openssh","collectionURL":"https://access.redhat.com/downloads/content/package-browser/","defaultStatus":"affected","cpes":["cpe:/o:redhat:enterprise_linux:10.0"],"versions":["unaffected 0:9.9p1-7.el10_0 <* (rpm)"]},{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9","packageName":"openssh","collectionURL":"https://access.redhat.com/downloads/content/package-browser/","defaultStatus":"affected","cpes":["cpe:/a:redhat:enterprise_linux:9::appstream","cpe:/o:redhat:enterprise_linux:9::baseos"],"versions":["unaffected 0:8.7p1-45.el9 <* (rpm)"]},{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9","packageName":"openssh","collectionURL":"https://access.redhat.com/downloads/content/package-browser/","defaultStatus":"affected","cpes":["cpe:/a:redhat:enterprise_linux:9::appstream","cpe:/o:redhat:enterprise_linux:9::baseos"],"versions":["unaffected 0:8.7p1-45.el9 <* (rpm)"]},{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 6","packageName":"openssh","collectionURL":"https://access.redhat.com/downloads/content/package-browser/","defaultStatus":"unaffected","cpes":["cpe:/o:redhat:rhel_els:6"]},{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 7","packageName":"openssh","collectionURL":"https://access.redhat.com/downloads/content/package-browser/","defaultStatus":"unaffected","cpes":["cpe:/o:redhat:rhel_els:7"]},{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 8","packageName":"openssh","collectionURL":"https://access.redhat.com/downloads/content/package-browser/","defaultStatus":"unaffected","cpes":["cpe:/a:redhat:enterprise_linux:8"]},{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat OpenShift Container Platform 4","packageName":"openshift/ose-rhel-coreos-8","collectionURL":"https://access.redhat.com/downloads/content/package-browser/","defaultStatus":"unaffected","cpes":["cpe:/a:redhat:openshift:4"]},{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat OpenShift Container Platform 4","packageName":"openshift/ose-rhel-coreos-9","collectionURL":"https://access.redhat.com/downloads/content/package-browser/","defaultStatus":"unaffected","cpes":["cpe:/a:redhat:openshift:4"]},{"vendor":"Siemens","product":"SIMATIC S7-1500 CPU 1518-4 PN/DP MFP","defaultStatus":"unknown","versions":["affected V3.1.0 <V3.1.5 (custom)"]},{"vendor":"Siemens","product":"SIMATIC S7-1500 CPU 1518F-4 PN/DP MFP","defaultStatus":"unknown","versions":["affected V3.1.0 <V3.1.5 (custom)"]},{"vendor":"Siemens","product":"SIPLUS S7-1500 CPU 1518-4 PN/DP MFP","defaultStatus":"unknown","versions":["affected V3.1.0 <V3.1.5 (custom)"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHBA-2025:6305","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHBA-2025:6305"},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2025:6993","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2025:6993"},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2025-26466","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_REDHAT"]},{"url":"https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2345043","tags":["issue-tracking","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHBZ#2345043"},{"url":"https://seclists.org/oss-sec/2025/q1/144"},{"url":"https://www.qualys.com/2025/02/18/openssh-mitm-dos.txt"},{"url":"https://security.netapp.com/advisory/ntap-20250228-0002/"},{"url":"https://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2025/02/18/1"},{"url":"https://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2025/02/18/4"},{"url":"https://bugzilla.suse.com/show_bug.cgi?id=1237041"},{"url":"https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2025-26466"},{"url":"https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2025-26466"},{"url":"http://seclists.org/fulldisclosure/2025/May/8"},{"url":"http://seclists.org/fulldisclosure/2025/May/7"},{"url":"http://seclists.org/fulldisclosure/2025/Feb/18"},{"url":"https://www.vicarius.io/vsociety/posts/cve-2025-26466-detection-script-memory-consumption-vulnerability-in-openssh"},{"url":"https://www.vicarius.io/vsociety/posts/cve-2025-26466-mitigation-script-memory-consumption-vulnerability-in-openssh"},{"url":"https://cert-portal.siemens.com/productcert/html/ssa-398330.html"}],"workarounds":["This issue can be mitigated by setting the following three different options in the sshd configuration file located at: /etc/ssh/sshd_config\n\nMaxStartups: Set to a reasonable value, this option controls the maximum number of concurrent unauthenticated connections the SSH server accepts;\n\nPerSourcePenalties: Set its suboptions to a reasonable value, this option is used to help sshd to detect and drop connections that are potentially malicious for the SSH server;\n\nLoginGraceTime: Set to a resonable value, this option controls how much time the SSH server will wait the client to authenticate before dropping its connection;\n\nAll the three option above needs to be set to implement a full mitigation for this vulnerability."],"vendors":["openssh"]}
{"id":"CVE-2025-32728","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2025-04-10T00:00:00.000Z","updated":"2026-10-15T01:06:04.078Z","description":"In sshd in OpenSSH before 10.0, the DisableForwarding directive does not adhere to the documentation stating that it disables X11 and agent forwarding.","cwe":["CWE-440 CWE-440 Expected Behavior Violation"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","v":"3.1","score":4.3,"sev":"MEDIUM","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:N/I:L/A:N"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"none","Automatable":"no","Technical Impact":"partial"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"OpenBSD","product":"OpenSSH","defaultStatus":"unaffected","versions":["affected 7.4 <10.0 (custom)"]},{"vendor":"Siemens","product":"SIMATIC S7-1500 CPU 1518-4 PN/DP MFP","defaultStatus":"unknown","versions":["affected V3.1.0 <V3.1.5 (custom)"]},{"vendor":"Siemens","product":"SIMATIC S7-1500 CPU 1518F-4 PN/DP MFP","defaultStatus":"unknown","versions":["affected V3.1.0 <V3.1.5 (custom)"]},{"vendor":"Siemens","product":"SIPLUS S7-1500 CPU 1518-4 PN/DP MFP","defaultStatus":"unknown","versions":["affected V3.1.0 <V3.1.5 (custom)"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://lists.mindrot.org/pipermail/openssh-unix-dev/2025-April/041879.html"},{"url":"https://www.openssh.com/txt/release-10.0"},{"url":"https://github.com/openssh/openssh-portable/commit/fc86875e6acb36401dfc1dfb6b628a9d1460f367"},{"url":"https://ftp.openbsd.org/pub/OpenBSD/patches/7.6/common/013_ssh.patch.sig"},{"url":"https://www.openssh.com/txt/release-7.4"},{"url":"https://security.netapp.com/advisory/ntap-20250425-0002/"},{"url":"https://lists.debian.org/debian-lts-announce/2025/05/msg00008.html"},{"url":"https://cert-portal.siemens.com/productcert/html/ssa-398330.html"}],"vendors":["openssh"]}
{"id":"CVE-2025-61984","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2025-10-06T00:00:00.000Z","updated":"2026-11-10T12:37:52.720Z","description":"ssh in OpenSSH before 10.1 allows control characters in usernames that originate from certain possibly untrusted sources, potentially leading to code execution when a ProxyCommand is used. The untrusted sources are the command line and %-sequence expansion of a configuration file. (A configuration file that provides a complete literal username is not categorized as an untrusted source.)","cwe":["CWE-159 CWE-159 Improper Handling of Invalid Use of Special Elements"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","v":"3.1","score":3.6,"sev":"LOW","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:N"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"poc","Automatable":"no","Technical Impact":"total"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"OpenBSD","product":"OpenSSH","defaultStatus":"unaffected","versions":["affected 0 <10.1 (custom)"]},{"vendor":"Siemens","product":"SIMATIC S7-1500 CPU 1518-4 PN/DP MFP (6ES7518-4AX00-1AB0)","defaultStatus":"unknown","versions":["affected V3.1.6 <* (custom)"]},{"vendor":"Siemens","product":"SIMATIC S7-1500 CPU 1518-4 PN/DP MFP (6ES7518-4AX00-1AB0)","defaultStatus":"unknown","versions":["affected V3.1.7 <* (custom)"]},{"vendor":"Siemens","product":"SIMATIC S7-1500 CPU 1518-4 PN/DP MFP (6ES7518-4AX00-1AC0)","defaultStatus":"unknown","versions":["affected V3.1.6 <* (custom)"]},{"vendor":"Siemens","product":"SIMATIC S7-1500 CPU 1518-4 PN/DP MFP (6ES7518-4AX00-1AC0)","defaultStatus":"unknown","versions":["affected V3.1.7 <* (custom)"]},{"vendor":"Siemens","product":"SIMATIC S7-1500 CPU 1518F-4 PN/DP MFP (6ES7518-4FX00-1AB0)","defaultStatus":"unknown","versions":["affected V3.1.6 <* (custom)"]},{"vendor":"Siemens","product":"SIMATIC S7-1500 CPU 1518F-4 PN/DP MFP (6ES7518-4FX00-1AB0)","defaultStatus":"unknown","versions":["affected V3.1.7 <* (custom)"]},{"vendor":"Siemens","product":"SIMATIC S7-1500 CPU 1518F-4 PN/DP MFP (6ES7518-4FX